# FreeRADIUS users for the campus lab.
#
# Authentication methods:
#   - staff/student/guest: EAP-MD5 (wpa_supplicant eap=MD5, see endpoints/client/)
#   - IoT sensors:         MAB (MAC Authentication Bypass); the MAC is both the
#                          RADIUS User-Name and the password Cisco IOS sends.
#
# Dynamic VLAN reply attributes required by the assignment:
#   Tunnel-Type               = VLAN
#   Tunnel-Medium-Type        = IEEE-802
#   Tunnel-Private-Group-Id   = <VLAN ID>
#
# The switch applies the VLAN because it has:
#   aaa authorization network default group radius
#
# PASSWORDS: change these together with radius/secrets.env and
# endpoints/client/wpa_supplicant-*.conf. tests/verify_configs.py checks them.
#
# MAC FORMAT: Cisco IOS MAB normally sends the MAC in dotted form, for example
# 0200.0000.4001. Aliases for the other common formats (plain 12 hex digits,
# hyphens, colons) are included at the end of this file. If `radiusd -X` shows
# a different User-Name format on your image (for example uppercase), add one
# alias for that exact string. The VLAN attributes stay the same.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STAFF -> VLAN 10
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
staff1  Cleartext-Password := "Staff1Pass!"
        Tunnel-Type = VLAN,
        Tunnel-Medium-Type = IEEE-802,
        Tunnel-Private-Group-Id = "10"

staff2  Cleartext-Password := "Staff2Pass!"
        Tunnel-Type = VLAN,
        Tunnel-Medium-Type = IEEE-802,
        Tunnel-Private-Group-Id = "10"

staff3  Cleartext-Password := "Staff3Pass!"
        Tunnel-Type = VLAN,
        Tunnel-Medium-Type = IEEE-802,
        Tunnel-Private-Group-Id = "10"

